Aerie-Purpose: Turn on strict HTTPS-only mode by default; the user can still change it in settings.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc (default of the https_only_mode_enabled pref)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Chromium skips the upgrade for localhost, 127.0.0.0/8, ::1 and *.localhost, so a dev
server on http://localhost:<port> still loads with no warning page. The settings radio
group reads the same pref, so it shows Always use secure connections without writing
anything. A choice the user makes in settings is written to the pref and then wins.

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
@@ -274,5 +274,5 @@
 
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
-      prefs::kHttpsOnlyModeEnabled, false,
+      prefs::kHttpsOnlyModeEnabled, true,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
